      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to find the value of \\( x \\) given the relationships between \\( x \\), \\( y \\), and \\( z \\), and the value of \\( z \\).\n\n1. **Identify the relationship between \\( x \\) and \\( y \\):**\n   The problem states that the value of \\( x \\) is one-half the value of \\( y \\). This can be written as:\n   \\[\n   x = \\frac{1}{2} y\n   \\]\n\n2. **Identify the relationship between \\( y \\) and \\( z \\):**\n   The problem also states that the value of \\( y \\) is one-fifth the value of \\( z \\). This can be written as:\n   \\[\n   y = \\frac{1}{5} z\n   \\]\n\n3. **Substitute the given value of \\( z \\):**\n   We are given that \\( z = 60 \\). Substitute \\( z = 60 \\) into the equation for \\( y \\):\n   \\[\n   y = \\frac{1}{5} \\times 60 = 12\n   \\]\n\n4. **Find the value of \\( x \\) using the relationship between \\( x \\) and \\( y \\):**\n   Now that we have \\( y = 12 \\), substitute this value into the equation for \\( x \\):\n   \\[\n   x = \\frac{1}{2} y = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 12 = 6\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\( x \\) is \\(\\boxed{6}\\).",
